+# v17.08-shared — follow-up A: the Lead Category job no longer asks GHL for its field list when nothing is queued
+
+Part of the CPU work (v17.07). Separate change; not part of the first 48-hour Orlando pilot.
+
+## Change
+- `leadCatBatch` (every 5-minute tick, every site): the pause check stays first; then the queue (`lead_cat_fix`,
+  up to 40 rows) is read BEFORE the GHL custom-field list. Empty queue → `{ done: 0, left: 0 }` at once (same result
+  as before when the field exists), no GHL request. Otherwise the rows already read are used.
+- Unchanged: return shape, pause result, "no Lead Category field" error when rows are waiting, 429 stops the batch,
+  400/404 drop the row, a row is deleted only if its category didn't change meanwhile (`WHERE ghl_id AND cat`).
+- Only difference: with an empty queue AND the field missing, the job no longer reports the missing field (it has
+  nothing to write).
+- Saves one GHL API call (custom-field list) plus parsing it on ~288 ticks a day per site whenever the queue is empty
+  — also GHL rate-limit budget. No observed queue writes in the 48 h baseline logs (no "Lead Category written" line).
+
+## Tests (scripts/qa/cron-cpu.test.mjs, fake GHL)
+- 9/9: empty (0 field lookups — fails on v17.07, 1 lookup), pending (1 lookup, 3 custom-field-only writes, rows
+  removed, same log line), paused, 429 (stops, nothing removed, retried next tick), missing field with a row queued.
+
+## Status
+- Committed on branch cpu-followups; not deployed.
